  ('zcrm_1579374000054719011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055112303', 'Scott Yarian', NULL, '7-28-20 Scott is 61 and wife is 59. Both have blood pressure meds and wife has anti-depressants. They do their wellness visits and have had an HSA in past, but used up funds. Understand value of HSA. Scott is looking at jobs and has one potential for employer who will offer health ins, but more likely will take a 1099 gig and need own healthcare. Sept 1st start date is only option. He already ran through 2 month wait period for Cobra and would owe about $6K if they back date if. So, no great solutions for Aug. but will deal with it on his own. They also have twins who are still dependents on his taxes. 3rd child is married and independent. One twin was in bad car accident and broke leg but other driver''s insurance is covering all cost of the broken leg. Looking at MPB Carez with MEC at $1000/$931.50.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-28 16:25:49', '2020-07-28 16:25:49'),
