  ('zcrm_1579374000054353034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010857102', 'Kimi Mischke', NULL, '7-21-20 Kimi chose MPB CareZ with MEC for wellness and HSA compliance. The only Need they were working towards was mental health for child. They didn''t reach their $500 IUA yet and she knows that starts over now and is $1000. So, may not reach that IUA but also knows if does, it''s shared up to $3K for that. No other known issues. She does want to get her mammogram and colonoscopy soon and I told her to call Concierge for assistance since she thinks her dr. is not in network. She will call to get help with that. All set. $1000/$931.50.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-21 16:09:41', '2020-07-21 16:09:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054353029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054394018', 'Kalen Ostrewich', NULL, '7-21-20 I called him back and explained SDHC for better rate. But, he realized this won''t work since he''s divorced and he''s legally required to pay for son''s health insurance. If ex-wife goes in as self-pay she will be stuck with the bill and that won''t work. It''s not ideal for his situation and he really only needs it for his son, not himself. So, none of these are ideal in this care. He''s also price sensitive without his job at the moment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-21 15:59:27', '2020-07-21 15:59:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054353024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054394018', 'Kalen Ostrewich', NULL, '7-21-20 Kalen has VA coverage and just quit job so lost that coverage. But, has 9 year old son he wants to get healthcare for. Son was born with a heart defect. Born with 2 flaps instead of 3. Was getting echo cardiogram once every year. Now doesn''t need one for 2-3 years. There is nothing to do about this defect other than to monitor it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-21 15:46:01', '2020-07-21 15:46:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054376013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521331', 'Vickie Peterson', NULL, 'Welcome Call Complete!  Mentioned Refferal.  KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-07-21 14:58:16', '2020-07-21 15:00:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054353013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919695', 'Erinn Magin', NULL, '7-21-20 Erinn is healthy, no pre-x and wants most similar to what she has now which is MPB CareZ with MEC. She funds an HSA already and will do her annual wellness visit this year as well. $1000/$294. She might need bunyon surgery sometime. Told her she will pay first $1000 and then shared up to $25K since sounds like pre-x. She understands.  I also told her to call Concierge if she needs help with that process.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-21 14:48:31', '2020-07-21 14:54:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054372013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, 'Patti tried calling her back to explain how her situation is going to work with her car accident incident and got her voicemail, Patti left a message. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-07-21 14:32:47', '2020-07-21 14:32:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054376008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013330029', 'Mary Suzanne Brauning', NULL, 'Welcome call complete.  Referral amount mentioned. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-07-21 14:24:05', '2020-07-21 14:24:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054376003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016068311', 'Jessica Bates', NULL, 'Welcome Call Complete! Mentioned Referral. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-07-21 13:58:42', '2020-07-21 13:58:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054353008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010543087', 'Tania Dibbs', NULL, 'Tania had hip replacement 1 year ago. Knows the pre-x clause with Zion at $25K year 1 and 2, $50K year 3, $125K year 4+ and doesn''t expect any major problems. No meds, except hormones. $2500/$319 MPB CareZ with MEC. Submitted. All set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-21 13:58:36', '2020-07-21 13:58:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054372008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054361023', 'Jared Stipic', NULL, 'Member Only $2500 IUA 18-29 MPB Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-07-21 13:56:49', '2020-07-21 13:56:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054372003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, 'Ticket was opened for member. I will paste what happened: 
I called Amber back and asked what type of appointment she is talking about because there is no authorization form to not have her pay. She explained that this was for a car accident she was in a few weeks ago and I stopped her and told her that the very first thing she is to do when it comes to car accidents is the at fault driver''s insurance. She then said she is so confused and asked me "So I am supposed all by myself try and get the money from the person''s insurance?
 I said yes not matter what that is the first thing that happens with car accidents. She said "I can tell you are getting frustrated and i am frustrated and none of this makes any sense". I said I am not getting frustrated I am just trying to give her the correct information. She than said she has an attorney and what not but does not have anything else or any forms from them for this, ect.. When I tried explaining everything to her and that she does not go through us or Sedera or anyone until after she has gone through the at fault''s car insurance. She then asked me if I were a regular health insurance company wouldn''t we get all the info from the car insurance for her and pay for it? I said I do not know because I do not work with regular health insurance and do not know that answer. I was in the middle of saying I was going to put her through to Patti that can better answer all of this for her and she said she is just going to go back to Blue Cross Blue Shield because none of this makes sense and that it is not fair that she has to do all of this on her own. She said ok about putting her through to Patti and then she hung up before Patti could answer her. I am going to try and have Patti call her back.  -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-07-21 13:56:09', '2020-07-21 13:56:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054340033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, 'Member called in and told Kelly F that she had been a car accident and that she needed us to pay.  I was unable to take the call and tried to call her back to explain to her that it would be the at fault driver''s Auto Ins PIP that would be primary and any coverage that she has would be secondary.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-07-21 13:34:08', '2020-07-21 13:34:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000054353003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015937096', 'Ramon Pinela', NULL, '7-21-20 Ramon said he wanted to keep his membership active even though Marie-Christine won''t pay for it since he left working for her unexpectedly. He and I had an appt yesterday and he didn''t answer. I had Marie-Christine submit a change form to remove her from his billed amount since she''s not responsible to pay for him Aug. 1st and beyond. I left him a vm yesterday and today. No answer. Patti is working on removing her payment information in Quickbooks so she''s not billed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-07-21 13:27:56', '2020-07-21 13:27:56'),
