  ('zcrm_1579374000052452003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045889059', 'David Norris', NULL, 'Member called in to update payment information I will send out link', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-06-16 09:45:11', '2020-06-16 09:45:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052419013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027741557', 'Ethan Pajak', NULL, 'Received newborn Gia SS# from Ethan.  I will send to Redirect.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-06-16 08:31:10', '2020-06-16 08:31:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052424003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029616183', 'Steven Caywood', NULL, 'Robin called in and said this is the first time her and her husband has had a plan like this and she needed to know what to do because she has an emergency with her knee and she can''t walk. I told her that anything with injury/illness she is responsible for paying the first $1500 out of pocket of her IUA. Anything after that is when she will need to get in contact with Sedera and open up a "Need". I told her if there is going to be surgery involved there is also another process she needs to go through with Sedera. I told her to call Sedera ASAP right when she gets off the phone with me and speak to someone over there that can help her with these process''s. She thanked me very much and hung up. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-06-16 07:17:27', '2020-06-16 07:17:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052419008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000009604129', 'Lori Frisbie', NULL, 'Lori called into request a list of Internist''s that are in network so that she can get follow up blood work associated with her older breast cancer diagnosis.  I explained to her the difference of preventative care and care for illness- she then asked if it would then be a covered expense from the original medical need.  I told her that it was a conversation that she needs to have with Sedera.  She told me that she would call them right after.  She asked what we DO cover- I then went over preventative care again, I told her that nothing is "covered" that she has a plan that has a MEC and for services to be $0 services need to be coded as preventative- not diagnostic to qualify.  I sent all 3 preventative care emails and went over them all in detail (per her request) then ran a search for Internal Medicine doctors (F) in her area.  I told her that just because a doctor is listed and she goes to them does not mean that it will be a "covered" expense- it depends of the private conversation that she and her doctor have.  I told her very clearly that blood work and tests related to a breast cancer diagnosis are not preventative in nature and wouldn''t be a $0 dollar expense.  It would be out of pocket. OR submitted to Sedera if there is already an open need. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-06-15 14:44:20', '2020-06-15 14:44:20'),
