  ('zcrm_1579374000052358003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045539150', 'maria molina', NULL, 'Ali and I  spoke to client....Client wanted to find Preventative Physician in local area...informed client to contact concierge dept.  Client said she would call.   Client also detailed that she did not complete enrollment herself...affiliate obtained CC# financial information and enrolled the client personally in enrollment system.', 'Guy Travis', 'Guy Travis', '2020-06-12 13:12:00', '2020-06-12 13:12:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052351013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050050129', 'Xavier Nogue', NULL, 'Member''s spouse called in and asked why he was not being billed.  John amd I looked inot this and member''s initial pmt declined so when Sunny collected pmt June pmt did not bill.  I told her that we could draft June Pmt and then July would draft on 6/20.  She ok with this.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-06-12 12:49:02', '2020-06-12 12:49:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052340010', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003848025', 'Jennika Wildau', NULL, 'Jennika called in regarding opening as need.  Had an overnight stay in the hospital along with multiple covid tests.  Explained that all bills are part of the same need.  open for as long as is necessary to reach curative state (2+yrs for example) different from deductible.  She had an understanding and this reinforced it.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2020-06-12 11:54:32', '2020-06-12 11:54:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052350008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740011', 'Kathleen VanGoethem', NULL, 'Kathleen called in and said she fell and broke her wrist yesterday and I explanied to her that is injury/illness and she is responsible for the first $1000 of her IUA anything after that she has to open a Need with Sedera. She knew all of that and confirmed their number. She then said well what if there needs to be surgery? I said that is still the same deal with meeting her IUA and that if there is any sort of surgery she needs to go through a process with Sedera and she needs to get a second opinion and she got very pissed off about that and said "Oh come on, are you Fing serious? It better not be a long process because I am 100% sure I need surgery and they are just going to do it, I can''t sit around and wait they are just going to do it." I told her I am sorry but that is the way it is if you want it to be covered. I told her to call Sedera ASAP and let them know everything she told me. She was all angry and huffy and puffy about needing a second opinion, she was cursing saying that''s ridiculous. You can''t make people wait if they need a surgery. I said that''s not what the process is, we don''t just make members sit around and wait, it is a very easy process you just have to do everything they say otherwise it will not be covered and she has to pay out of pocket for it all if she does not go through the process. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-06-12 11:37:04', '2020-06-12 11:37:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052351008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610322', 'Patricia Whitmer', NULL, 'Per Sedera''s requested requested updated Proof of DPC from Member', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-06-12 11:18:59', '2020-06-12 11:18:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052351003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610002', 'Deborah Vaughan', NULL, 'Per request from Sedera I requested an update Proof of DPC from this member.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-06-12 11:14:15', '2020-06-12 11:14:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000052350003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016038088', 'Lisa Campbell', NULL, 'Lisa called in and said that she has "Insurance" with Sedera and she went to her yearly wellness visit and then was told her has APEX and she called APEX and they said they do not know who she is and is not in their system. I pulled up her profile here and she does not have a MEC, she has no preventative coverage. She had no clue what I was talking about so I have Patti explain to her further and that she used to be on the ASI plan but cancelled in March of 2019 and enrolled in this plan the Self-Directed with NO MEC. So she is responsible out of pocket to pay for her visit. The only thing she has that would be covered would be a Mammogram and a Colonoscopy as long as she is over 50 years old and those are covered through Sedera. She was not too happy about any of this and Patti let her know that she can NOT re enroll in the APEX plan because that is closed, we do not sell that anymore. Patti advised Lisa get with Kevin Michaels to discuss other options for her. -KF/PB', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-06-12 11:14:11', '2020-06-12 11:14:11'),
