  ('zcrm_1579374000051679019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026991117', 'Ryan Dunlap', NULL, 'called to ask how to get started with Cirrus MD, he never received an invitation.  I sent him the invitation, his information wasn''t being found.  His daughter burned her finger with a hot glue gun and they wanted to know if they needed to go to an urgent care or not.  I told Ryan that it was after hours but there might be a chance that John reaches out tonight...I slacked John this request. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-29 18:19:08', '2020-05-29 18:19:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000051679013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031044058', 'Samantha Midler', NULL, 'Josh from Sedera transferred Samantha over to me, saying that she had called Apex about a preventative bill and the claim was being denied, so she tried to submit it to Sedera and Josh explained that she couldn''t because she has a MEC, he asked me to explain the plan to her.  That is what I did.  Poor Samantha was completely confused about how her plan did or didn''t work.  It turns out that her doctor was not in network, and I had to break it to her that her bill would not be covered.  She understood, but was very frustrated that everything I was explaining to her she had never heard before, I told her that she did have a welcome call, but she didn''t ever receive the email that I had just sent her while.  She said that all the rest of the emails that she has gotten from us are just "fluff" and not the critical information as was being shown in that preventative care email that she was reading on the other end.  I sympathized with her, and told her that I understood her point of view.  She suggested that we send emails such as this to the members MONTHLY to remind them how to do these types of things because it is an extremely confusing plan that no one can possibly understand.  I told her that I would let my supervisor know about all of this, that I was going to send her the rest of the educational emails that I had, and suggested that she try to negotiate the bill with her doctors office.  I slacked Dania after the call to send a message to Josh about how the call went, and I asked if Karris could try negotiating the bill down on Samantha''s behalf.  Dania said that they definitely could try- I told Dania that it would mean a lot to Samantha if they would. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-29 17:27:53', '2020-05-29 17:56:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000051679008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006176011', 'Dona Tolan', NULL, 'Dona called in for help with a prescription for her son who has a bad ear infection.  She asked the doctor for the same medication that helped him previously.  The script was for Ciprodex- there is no generic, he needed it immediately,  the nurse had given her a coupon that would allow her to pick it up for $260- I did find something a tad bit expensive $234.60 , she was really grateful for that.  Super sweet about it- I told her that if there was more time Reid probably would''ve been able to do better.  She understood and was thankful. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-29 16:04:58', '2020-05-29 16:04:58'),
