  ('zcrm_1579374000050925008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011019034', 'Cheryl Cunningham', NULL, 'Spoke to Cheryl.  She loves us and wishes she didn''t have to go on Medicare.  There is not much we can do for her.  See ticket.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2020-05-11 17:52:41', '2020-05-11 17:52:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050948013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028257470', 'Claudia Nanino', NULL, '5-11-20 Claudia just lost her job and re-enrolled today for same membership as before PSDHC at $1000 IUA/ $296. I explained the new Virtual Healthcare and she sounded very excited about it. Told her to do the Welcome Call in order to set it up and refresh her memory about how it all works again. She will.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-11 16:52:35', '2020-05-11 16:52:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050948008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050956676', 'Elizabeth Card', NULL, '5-11-20 Liz works closely with Nate Butryn as her mentor and he recommended MPB to her. She works hard to keep in good health with nutrition, water, exercising, etc. No health issues, no meds, no tobacco. She''s 34 turning 35 this year. She uses a holistic Dr. Bill Cunningham who does biofeedback and is in Lafayette.  Doesn''t have ins at the moment. Has done wellness visit and is due for one. But has gone to Boulder Health Group and paid cash in the past and is willing to do so again. PSDHC isn''t worth the extra monthly fee for her at her age. She enrolled today on first call for SDHC at $1000/$221 for June 1st start date. She says this works similar to their pet insurance for their dog but couldn''t remember name of company.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-11 16:48:49', '2020-05-11 16:48:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050949013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048514273', 'Fang Xue', NULL, 'Welcome call complete.  She had a pretty good understanding, slightly overwhelmed but knows she can call for support any time.  She wants to know if a covid vax would be a covered preventive expense in the future and also if she will be exempt from the CA tax by having this plan. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-11 15:48:38', '2020-05-11 15:48:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050949008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993452', 'Holly Wiese', NULL, 'I have sent the following email to Holly and she is going to relay it to Greg-
Good Morning Kelly,

 

I called the provider this morning and spoke to Morgan in the billing department.  She said that since this is a limited plan they cannot fax or e-mail the itemized bill to us but if Greg calls them and requests it a copy would be mailed directly to him with the procedure codes and diagnosis codes.  Once he receives it he can fax it or e-mail to us.  The statement attached does show that a payment was made of $927.46 so if he would like payment made directly to him once he submits the bill and we have it priced he would need to indicate that on the bill.

 

Thank you.

 

 

Due to the Shelter in Place order issued by the City of Fresno, our office is now operating remotely.

 

We do not anticipate delays in our response time, however, if this should occur, please know that we are committed to maintaining our standard of customer service during this crisis and are doing our best to minimize disruptions to our clients, members and brokers.

 

We appreciate your patience and understanding during this very fluid situation.

 


<1.png>
	

    Kareen Rogers

     Account Representative

    
    Administrative Solutions
  o. (559) 256-1320 | f. (559) 475-5780

  www.asibenefits.com |  krogers@asibenefits.com

ASi office hours are 8:00am – 5:00pm Monday through Thursday, and 8:00am – 3:00pm on Fridays.', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-11 14:56:56', '2020-05-11 14:56:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050949003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046217082', 'Aaron Martin', NULL, 'Jenny called to get some questions regarding her plan answered, she had a pretty good grasp already- I just filled in the gaps.  Sent all preventive care templates and added her email address. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-11 13:42:12', '2020-05-11 13:42:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050940003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048549313', 'April Mestas', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-05-11 11:41:51', '2020-05-11 11:41:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050928003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000191454', 'Jennifer McMahon', NULL, 'Member wanted to change payment info, Sent form', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2020-05-11 09:41:26', '2020-05-11 09:41:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050925003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012416075', 'Katherine Richardson', NULL, 'Kate called in and instantly just asked to speak to John. I told her that he has been working remotely and I will try and transfer her over, she than said well I have his cell phone number can I just call that? I said if you have that number than yes of course you can call it. She immediately just said ok and hung up. She sounded pretty frustrated or in a hurry.  -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-05-11 09:06:19', '2020-05-11 09:06:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050910003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012010011', 'Elizabeth Wood', NULL, 'Elizabeth called in and said that she needs a routine colonoscopy and wanted to call in here first before she went to and appointment she already made and she told them that she is self pay. I let her know that is not correct and she is ONLY self pay when it is something with Injury/Illness. I explained how the whole process works with her preventative care and needing to stay in the PHCS network for anything preventative. I also told her about her RCI card and how that works and what she needs to do with that card upon arrival at her appt. I took down the facility and providers name that she made the appt. with and I will look that up, if they are NOT in the network than she needs to choose from the list I will send her for providers in her area. She was perfectly fine will all this and is happy she called here first before she just went to the appt she scheduled. She is going to call them and tell them to hold off for now until she figures how to go about it. I am sending her the general education emails about what to do with this type of appt. How to present her card upon arrival, 5 steps on how to avoid surprise bills for preventative care. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-05-11 08:40:14', '2020-05-11 08:40:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050897003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005591031', 'Bryan Holland', NULL, 'Member submitted Member Change form w/change of address.  I will update.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-05-11 07:13:11', '2020-05-11 07:13:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050870018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993452', 'Holly Wiese', NULL, 'Leena got back to me and let me know that they had never received the bill that Holly emailed me, so she is having someone from home office reach out to the provider on Monday and ask that they submit the bill. I let Holly know about this.- KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-08 16:57:18', '2020-05-08 16:57:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050870008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993452', 'Holly Wiese', NULL, 'Holly called because her husband received a labratory bill and they thought it would be covered as part as their preventative benefits.  I asked her to take pictures of the bill in question and send it in, and that if it had enough information that I would send it to ASI.  I asked if Greg had given his ASI card to the doctors and he told me that he had. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-08 15:45:59', '2020-05-08 15:45:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050875003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047084237', 'Mark DeRespinis', NULL, '5-8-20 Called Patti on Wed. 5/6 and she said John was working on this. Called John now and refreshed John about the wrong billed amount for Mark. John now remembers and will work on it right away. Mark is owed for 2 months that was billed for the wrong amount. 

Greetings Wendy,

I’m just checking in about my empowering benefits plan. We discussed adjusting the plan when the whole covid thing happened in order to reduce my monthly expenses. When we spoke I understood that the payment would be reduced to around $430 from the current $660. Since then, I have been charged twice, at the original unadjusted amount. I’ve been running around like a mad man trying to keep my business afloat, but I’d really like to address why this hasn’t gone into effect, and receive credit for the difference over the last two months.
Thank you
Mark DeRespinis', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-08 14:04:38', '2020-05-08 14:04:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050870003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027786019', 'Amber Senator', NULL, 'a labratory called to verify benefits with US.  I told them that they needed to reach back out to Amber and ask for RCI''s contact information. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-05-08 13:00:41', '2020-05-08 13:00:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050869003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008282039', 'Melissa Harper', NULL, 'Returned David''s, cal, left message, sent email.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2020-05-08 12:46:03', '2020-05-08 12:46:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050850003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447318', 'Laurel Kelner', NULL, 'Curtis the husband called in and said he needs to make a payment. I asked him what kind of payment because payments for the monthly premium automatically comes out as direct deposit. He said he knows that but needs to change the account it comes out of for the next few months. Put him through to Sunny. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-05-08 11:16:20', '2020-05-08 11:16:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050833014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447318', 'Laurel Kelner', NULL, 'Curtis Kelner called and wanted to make two payments (June and July) out of his business account. I processed 2 payments ($1140) on 5/8 and put the 5.22 and 6.22 payments on HOLD on FTNI. Regular reoccurring payments will continue normally again starting on 7.22. 

