  ('zcrm_1579374000050538003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050550098', 'Sarah Price', NULL, '4-30-20 Sarah enrolled in PDHC for June 1st start date. Sarah is admittedly overweight in the 25-30 BMI range but is working to get weight under control. It''s better than it was. She takes Lexipro for anxiety and progesterone cream for perimenopause. Otherwise, no issues on her end. Her 9 year old daughter has a processing disorder/brain development delay. I skimmed the guidelines and I don''t believe any of her visits will be shareable for that. She is already paying for all of it on her own and understands she will most likely continue to do so. She typically does annual wellness visits. Just got disenchanted bc mammograms come out uncertain bc she has dense breast tissue. So, she''s done the further exams and paid $800-$1000 for them to tell her everything is fine. She got tired of that and skipped a year.  We talked extensively about the pre-x clause and she understands a diagnostic scan is not preventative and therefore her responsibility to pay. She gets it. All set and appreciative. Also is working on new biz where collaborating about how to work together in times of need like pandemic for how we can become self sufficient and rely on one another for basic needs. Her expertise is in working/selling solar systems. I gave her permission to let me know more information about her business as she gets it going. Sounds intriguing.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-30 12:07:01', '2020-04-30 12:48:43'),
