  ('zcrm_1579374000050505003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073887226', 'Dennis Barela', NULL, 'Email sent by Sedera to this member advised that dependent would be removed from plan due the the fact that he would be aging out of plan. I will cancel in RCI and adjust billing', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-04-30 08:14:44', '2020-04-30 08:14:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050468008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000049932072', 'Akiaahia Proctor', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-04-30 07:59:08', '2020-04-30 07:59:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050493003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046483021', 'Rochelle Kirkwood', NULL, 'finished and sent prescription quote request off to Rochelle.  I spoke to Guy about the vitamin D- and he told me to have her ask her pharmacist about the strength and get a recommendation for something over the counter. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-04-29 18:18:15', '2020-04-29 18:18:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050463008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000052864149', 'Catherine Brown', NULL, '4-29-20 Husband just got laid off. Cathy is 53, Jeff is 53 and kids 18 and 16, Owen and Anna, not sure which one is which age. Anna takes 20 mg of fluoxetine (generic for Prozac) for anxiety and has asthma and food allergies. Also takes generic of Advair bc Advair is so expensive. She understands if Anna winds up in hospital for asthma/allergies they will be responsible for full cost of visit. She''s willing to take that risk. Anna hasn''t been hospitalized since she was really young. Cathy also takes 10 mg of Lexipro for anxiety. No tobacco and no other health issues. Dog even has anxiety she said. Sharing with her husband and enrolling tomorrow at noon.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-29 12:27:09', '2020-04-29 12:28:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050468003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048462092', 'Delia Villarreal-Webb', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-04-29 12:08:58', '2020-04-29 12:08:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050465003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044571112', 'Cheryl Claman-Brennan', NULL, 'Kayla Moon over at Sedera sent a slack message stating Cheryl contacted Sedera on how to cancel her membership. I called Cheryl and left a voice mail explaining what I am going to do by sending her an email with the cancellation link to fill out the form. I let her know on the message to get the form in before the 20th of next month due to that being the time we start billing for next months coverage. Sent cancellation email. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-04-29 12:01:10', '2020-04-29 12:01:10');
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000050463003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050550098', 'Sarah Price', NULL, '4-29-20 Sarah is 46 and daughter is 9. No insurance now bc hates system and boycotting it. They are self pay now and like the concept of MCS. Sending her the audio and we will talk tomorrow at 11:00.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-29 11:53:14', '2020-04-29 11:53:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050452008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050557009', 'Bridger Clifford', NULL, '4-29-20 Bridger can get Humira possibly at no cost via their My Abbvie program - abbvie.com/mypap. As long as he makes less than $75K annually and more than Medicaid level he should be accepted. He can only apply when he doesn''t have insurance. Therefore he must wait until May 1sts to apply when his parents plan ends. If he gets a STM plan then it can''t include meds or if it does include meds the co-pay is super high for Specialty drugs. The other option is to wait until June 1st to apply for the Abbvie program. It takes 3-4 business days to process the approval or denial. His doctor will have to complete 1 page as well. Approval = $0 for meds. His income is expected to be at $25K in 2020. He knows he will pay for dermatologist that he sees at University of Utah. He thinks the price might be reasonable since a U of U Dr.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-29 11:14:23', '2020-04-29 11:14:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050453003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919192', 'Tanya Bell', NULL, 'Charged the correct $322 for May and fixed rate for future payments to be drafted from the newly provided bank account', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2020-04-29 10:17:04', '2020-04-29 10:17:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050452003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919192', 'Tanya Bell', NULL, '4-29-20 Spoke with Sunny and Lucius and chose to use checking account to avoid fees. Charging correct amount now at $322 for her age turning 51 in June. Looks like never was charged correct amount when turned 50. Strange bc may have been 50 when she joined. Sunny will cross check everything.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-29 10:15:02', '2020-04-29 10:15:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050436008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026991007', 'Stephen Gonzales', NULL, 'Steve called in and said he needs a replacement ASi card sent to him asap because he is having preventative blood work done and his provider and the LabCorp need his ID number and everything to be able to send it out to the right place. I told him I would email the ID department at ASi and tag him in the email as well for a PDF copy emailed to him and a hard copy mailed to him. He was very happy that I could do that for him. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-04-29 08:44:56', '2020-04-29 08:44:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050436003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031904135', 'Rene Perdue', NULL, 'Member called in and requested proof of cancellation for Cigna.  I sent email stating that membership in Assoc was cancelled eff 1/1/2020 and that one of the benefit of that membership was membership in Medical Cost Sharing plan.  I emailed.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-04-29 08:12:31', '2020-04-29 08:12:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050407013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046514182', 'Jordan Kirkwood', NULL, 'Welcome call complete- from Jordan''s mom Rochelle''s notes-

Welcome call complete, she had her son Jordan join.  It became apparent that there may be some issue because Jordan asked if he could see his behavioral health doctor with his RCI card (he asked if he was in network and told me that is who prescribes him his medication)  Rochelle asked if any of his behavioral health would be a covered service- then asked if the medications would be covered.  I told her that besides the behavioral health offered at a discount through Sedera via Teladoc- everything else would be out of pocket.  She sounded really let down.  I then continued- I asked if they understood the pre x clause, she said yes, and Jordan said no- that''s when I went over it and she was completely shocked and said she didn''t hear it "put like that".  At the end of the welcome call she said she had some concerns, especially about the mental health aspect- she was also wondering how she would pay for her own therapist if she needed to reach out for help.  I told her that I understood her concerns, and empathized with her.  I am going to reach out to Guy about this situation. - KC

Contact -
Rochelle Kirkwood
