  ('zcrm_1579374000050406003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050557009', 'Bridger Clifford', NULL, '4-28-20 Bridger just turned 26 and is no longer on parents plan. He''s healthy but he does have psoriasis. Taking Humira which is over $5K but he gets it with Humira prescription card for $5! He''s checking to see if he can use that card without insurance or with any insurance. Takes 1 pen every 2 weeks 40mg/.4ml, citrate free. 2 single doses in pre-filled pen in one pack. Looked at coverage through University of UT for $330 a month and $5 for his me med with card. Waiting to hear from Reid about his option. June 1st is earliest start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-28 14:24:09', '2020-04-28 14:24:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050387011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919192', 'Tanya Bell', NULL, '4-28-20 Lucius Ashby called to provide payment for Tanya Bell. They pay with their firms cc. I will give it to Sunny to update account. I quoted him $322 a month and need to verify with Sunny at the $1500 IUA for PSDHC.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-28 12:32:31', '2020-04-28 12:32:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050387003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050370005', 'Arian Shirakhoon', NULL, '4-28-20 Arian is enrolled in Cigna Connect Flex Silver 2750 RX EPO. Her cost is $232.56 and APTC is $110.17 for total $342.73. Her job and insurance ended on 4/21/20. She was making about $69K per year. Her new unemployment amount will be $618 a week which is $32,136 annualized. She also just moved here from AZ about 1 year ago it sounds like. She was afraid to use C4 bc she had a bad experience in AZ with getting put onto Medicaid or Access as I think they call it, which she didn''t want. Anyhow, she finally understood she should apply through C4 since her income is now low enough to gain subsidy. She understands she must notify me or C4 if/when her income changes and she gets a new job. But, for now gets a subsidy and chose Cigna bc doesn''t like HMO''s and was afraid of Bright Health bc not familiar with it. She knows to make sure she doesn''t need a referral if wants to see specialist. She will double check. She made her first pmt with cc and knows to set up ongoing payments once receives info from Cigna. We spoke with Malaysia with C4 who helped us complete the application bc Arian''s name wasn''t accepted on app each time. Just copied and pasted the name and then it worked. Malaysia confirmed start date will be 5/1/20. All set! Arian will recommend me to others since I was so helpful.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-28 12:02:18', '2020-04-28 12:02:18'),
