  ('zcrm_1579374000049075018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000049054188', 'Chris Larson', NULL, 'Member &amp; SP $5000 IUA 60-64 PSD', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-03-31 11:43:04', '2020-03-31 11:43:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000049075013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000049054126', 'Santiago Mussi Tiscornia', NULL, 'Member Only $2500 30-39 SD', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-03-31 11:34:17', '2020-03-31 11:34:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000049075008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018402156', 'Jeanette Malki', NULL, 'Member called in and said that she has gotten mutiple bill from her labs.  I asked if this had been submitted to ASi she said mutiple times.  She also said that she made sure that it was coded correctly. I advised her that ASi was in lockdown and could not give her any timeframe  for a response.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-03-31 11:31:08', '2020-03-31 11:31:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000049076033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010954128', 'Brent Toevs', NULL, 'Called in to make sure that her address was correct because she sent in an address change form. Everything was correct, Patti changed everything Feb 14th. Also wanted to know what to do because she is starting to get the bills in from an emergency room visit for he daughter. I told her that she is supposed to present herself as cash pay and she said she did. I let her know she is responsible for the first $1000 and then the rest is supposed to be submitted to Sedera and start a "Need". She fully understood and I sent her an email that explains how to submit the bills along with Sedera''s phone number. I advised her to call Sedera asap since she is getting the bills in now. She will call now. Was very thankful for all the help! -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-03-31 11:23:30', '2020-03-31 11:23:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000049076028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008628057', 'Anthony Belisle', NULL, 'From Ticket for today 3/31/20: 

I called Tony back and he had his wife on the line as well and they wanted to make sure it was ok that they were switching their pharmacy from Walmart to Walgreens. I said um yeah but I don''t understand why you are calling into here to tell me this. There is no coverage on your plan with prescriptions. I began to explain what we do when it comes to finding prescription coupons. The wife cut me off and said well excuse me if I am ignorant but on the back of the card it says to have the pharmacist submit prescriptions with an IBM number. I transferred the call to Patti because I did not know what that meant. Patti explained that prescriptions are only shared when it has something to do with a "Need". What is says on the back of the ASi card is only if you are using the injury/illness part of ASi but they are not supposed to because they use Sedera. The wife then said well we get it for Free at Walmart through the card. She thought that because of what it says on the back of the card and the fact that they show their card when they pick up their prescriptions it was Free with coverage. Patti explained that Walmart is the one that has that specific medication for free. It has nothing thing to do with the card and said to never ever show the card when picking up prescriptions. Everything is cash pay, unless it pertains to a "Need" with Sedera. Patti advised that they stay with Walmart since they have it for free and not switch over to Walgreens because it probably will not be free with them. All in all the members were confused and thought that they are supposed to show their ASi card when picking up prescriptions and they get coverage. Patti made sure they understand now. All Set. Ticket Closed. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-03-31 10:45:15', '2020-03-31 10:45:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000049087003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030348722', 'Tamara Orebaugh', NULL, 'Welcome call complete with new plan. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-03-31 10:38:28', '2020-03-31 10:38:28'),
