  ('zcrm_1579374000047543003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016721056', 'Susan Crocker', NULL, 'I called Monica Lugo at ASI to get an update about Susan''s $1529.30 Lab work bill that she sent me Jan 28th. The reason being is, Susan got another bill stating that she still owed the full amount this time (the first bill had a $333.38 credit taken off) because the facility was not in network. The facility sent her this notice stating they are not in the PHCS network. I checked again to see if they are and they ARE and Monica Lugo also while on the phone with me said they most certainly are. So Monica told me that a check for $1146.24 was sent out Feb 4th to Good Samaritan Medical Center and there is a note on there that says they have to write off the other $382.06 because they ARE in the network. Monica reassured me that regardless everything is going to be paid because if not then she is going to have to get the network involved to get it paid off fully. Susan will not owe anything and Monica told me to let Susan know if she keeps getting billed to let her know and they will take care of it. Susan and her husband can breath now! I asked Monica if she could shoot an email to Susan putting in words everything she told me just so Susan can have it in wording as proof. She is very very very very good about keep any and ALL paper work and all emails. I called Susan back to let her know the good news and she was nearly in tears of happiness. She literally had nothing to say for a few seconds because she was so relieved. Susan is very very thankful and just so happy now because that was a HUGE amount owed and her and her husband didn''t know how to come up with that. She said her day has been made and she is just so very thankful for everything I did to help her and get this lab work paid off. She is all set!! :) :) -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-02-26 13:25:27', '2020-02-26 13:25:27'),
