  ('zcrm_1579374000047469017', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026552012', 'Karen W. Isaac', NULL, 'Karen called in and she needs to change her address and also change her credit card information. I sent her over to Patti because she is the one that has the forms she needs to send out to her. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-02-26 08:15:21', '2020-02-26 08:15:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047469003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011899314', 'Timothy Sparrow', NULL, 'Karen called and asked if she needed to inform us that she was going to her preventative visit.  I told her no as long as she knew the dr was in network.  Also asked about 2nd knee replacement surgery for her daughter in May and I advised her about 2nd md and to start the needs process.  I gave her the contact number and told her to call. - PB', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-02-26 07:56:04', '2020-02-26 07:56:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047453026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017126041', 'Steven Strehlow', NULL, 'I just realized that Julie probably never even had a welcome call, because she was added later to the plan.  I will ask John about this....- KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-25 16:51:49', '2020-02-25 16:51:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047453021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045539203', 'Shine Paul', NULL, 'email I sent to Patti and Sunny after my call with Shine-

...Shine is VERY upset that his money hasn''t been taken out of his account for this month.  Upset that I couldn''t tell him if he paid last month. 

He grilled me on where we were located- and then specifically our time zone.  I told him that I did not see any red flags or notes on his account and assured him that someone in finance was going to contact him in the morning about this.

He thought that this was an emergency that you all needed to be called on, and I tried my best to let him know that it''s all going to be fine, and that you would touch bases with him in the morning.

-KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-25 16:49:46', '2020-02-25 16:49:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047453013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017126041', 'Steven Strehlow', NULL, 'Julie called in stating that Steven needs to go see a cardiologist and will probably need a stress test, and other very expensive tests (she rattled off about 3 of them) "to get a baseline" and then "that''ll be covered as preventative right?"  I explained to her that it would NOT, and then I mentioned that he may be able to submit it as a medical need with Sedera as long as this is a newer need.  She then said that her husband has high blood pressure but that he takes medication for it, and that, she flippantly stated he was "old".....and then something about high blood pressure and being old go hand in hand.  I then told her that the BEST idea for her would be to give Sedera a phone call about this, and told her that you could ask about the need being shareable AND have them help find the best price and place for Steven to receive these tests.  I gave her their number.  She then asked about her well womens visit and a mammogram- I went over all protocol verbally as well as sent her 3 emails and stressed the importance of them.  
She was very rude and didn''t really care to know how anything worked.  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-25 16:26:03', '2020-02-25 17:07:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047438013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047639040', 'Keegan Swenson', NULL, '2-25-20 Keegan just turned 26 on Feb. 16th, 2020. He''s healthy, no tobacco and booted off parents ins at end of month. Missed deadline for March 1st start. He will get https://www.lifebyspot.com to get him protected up to $20K. But, my STM and Accident Policies aren''t in UT. Todd Cloward''s STM doesn''t start until May 1st. I Found some solutions on ehealthinsurance through National General if need be.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-25 16:11:57', '2020-02-25 16:11:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047453008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044904687', 'Mike Gardner', NULL, 'Welcome call complete.  Many questions, eager to learn, I assured him that we will be here to guide him through the entire process.- KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-25 15:36:57', '2020-02-25 15:36:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047438008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047238442', 'Anne DeWaters', NULL, '2-25-20 Annie called wanting to know if her membership included access to Urgent Care. I left her a vm explaining that if they can treat it over the phone they''ll connect her to a Dr. If not, she will need to pay as a self-pay patient. She says she has the flu.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-25 15:15:25', '2020-02-25 15:15:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047453003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011083120', 'Margaret Noonan', NULL, 'Margaret Noonan called in about her husbands tennis elbow that he is going to go to physical therapy for.  She said that the total hasn''t yet gone over yet,  the doctor''s visits and imaging.  I told her that she needs to call Sedera as soon as the amount goes over, or if she is thinking it will.  She then spoke about an injection that her husband was going to get that "probably wouldn''t be covered" - I told her not to be so sure and if the husband is planning on getting this stem cell based $500 injection that Sedera needed to be aware of this.  I stressed this to her several times and made sure that she had their phone number.  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-25 14:45:34', '2020-02-25 14:45:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047427031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033185042', 'Lynn Quire', NULL, 'Lynn called in and stated that she needed help with getting a colonoscopy scheduled or at least just making sure that she is not loosing her mind and is doing the correct thing. She absolutely is doing the correct thing by calling into here and making sure. I went over the process with her about making sure the facility AND provider are in the PHCS Network, which I doubled checked and they both are so she is good to go on that part. I also let her know that, and obviously she won''t know now because she does not know who the anesthesiologist is yet, but she needs to make sure they are in the network as well when she is getting it done but simply asking and or getting their name and then I can look it up for her. She totally understood that. Next I went over her RCI card with her while she was looking at it during our call and went over the 2 phone numbers on the back of the card that the front desk will call to verify her benefits, lastly the P.O. Box address right next to the customer service #''s, is where she has the billing dept. submit the claims to. I made sure it is VERY important that they submit everything into that address and not just bill her. She understood everything I told her and was perfectly fine with everything. She stated at the end of everything that when she calls the facility to make her appt. they will not make one for her b/c they said they don''t like the "Insurance" and says it is not real "Insurance" and what not. I explained to her that this happens all the time and they are correct in the fact that yes, this is NOT Insurance, it is Medical Cost Sharing. But the reason for the phone numbers I went over with her on her RCI card is to fix this issue and they are to call those #''s and it goes directly to RCI and they will verify her benefits to whomever is calling. That should solve their issue right then and there. She also stated that they have her card on file already and I told her that is fine but to still physically always show the card because some things could have gotten lost or written down wrong in their system so it is just safe to always show the card. She 100% agreed and understood everything I went over with her. She was very very happy for all the help and reassuring her that she was doing everything the right way and is indeed NOT loosing her mind haha. Very happy and satisfied member. Hopefully after calling them back and telling them that I helped her and tell them to call those 2 #''s to verify the benefits will solve her issue and they will make an appt. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-02-25 12:49:51', '2020-02-25 12:49:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047432038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011752018', 'Kim Rust', NULL, 'Member submitted a Member change form to remove spouse.  I will notify ASi &amp; Sedera and change &amp; refund difference.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-02-25 12:15:29', '2020-02-25 12:15:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047427026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047238442', 'Anne DeWaters', NULL, 'Anne called in and asked if her $100 prescription is covered with her plan, she said she is new and did not know. She had Redirect so I told her that they are her first point of contact for ANYTHING . When I said Redirect her response was "What does that mean, what is that?" Which alarms me greatly b/c that is her entire plan, she should not be asking those questions. To me that tells me she has no idea what she signed p for. I briefly explained that Redirect is her plan and they are the ones she should be calling for anything and everything with her plan. She said ok and I asked if she could hold for a moment because I let her know I was not sure about prescriptions with Redirect so I was going to ask Patti the group admin if there is anything special with prescription''s when having Redirect, Patti said "Well first off she does not start until March 1 so we can not help her or let her utilize anything just yet, but yes after she starts March 1st it is the same as everything else where there is the prescription quote form for her to fill out and submit back to us and I will look around for coupon''s and send the coupons I find over to her via email. But for now she has to pay for everything she has done medically out of pocket and no she will NOT be reimbursed because she has not started with us yet. She understood. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-02-25 11:30:34', '2020-02-25 11:30:34'),
