  ('zcrm_1579374000047162008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038529351', 'Rebecca Stirling', NULL, 'I got a claim form sent in the mail to us in regards to some sort of appointment that Rebecca went to. It seems she gave the clinic out information and had everything sent to us. I emailed Rebecca that this was not supposed to come to us and that she HAS to have anything and everything approved by Redirect before she goes and gets anything done. I told her that Redirect is the carrier that she has and they are the ones that pick the doctors and make the appointments for her. She can not just go and have anything done wherever she wants. I told her that there is nothing I can do with what was sent to us and that she needs to get in contact with Redirect asap and let them know what happened and I also told her to contact this providers office and let them know to send the claim to Redirect and not us. I fair warned her too in the email that this is most likely not going to be covered because she did not go through Redirect, and is giving the wrong info out to providers. She thinks we are her "Insurance" carriers and the people that take care of everything. She has called us numerous times thinking we are the people she needs to speak to. We have always let her know every time that she needs to contact Redirect! She does not seem to understand that still. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-02-19 08:41:22', '2020-02-19 08:41:22'),
