  ('zcrm_1579374000047071051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047084237', 'Mark DeRespinis', NULL, 'Member &amp; Ch $500 IUA 40-49 Redirect', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-02-17 13:06:56', '2020-02-17 13:06:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047092008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047084237', 'Mark DeRespinis', NULL, '2-17-20 Mark enrolled him and his daughter in PDHC bc daughter gets sick on occasion and they go to dr. about 6x per year. Putting Tara onto trad insurance but they need the Medicaid denial first to proceed on that end. Mark chose the $500 IUA/$607 month for Parent/Child.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-17 12:46:43', '2020-02-17 12:46:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000047092003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048541002', 'Tara Lanich-LaBrie', NULL, '2-17-20 Tara is married to Mark DeRespinis. Tara has heart palpitations they are looking into but say is fine, had a breast biopsy they are keeping an eye on for future cancer,  but none now and has polycystic ovarian syndrome ongoing. Not a good candidate for MCS. Choosing Cigna Silver with $2750 Ded/$8150 mop. She will lose her Dr. Holly Ann Powell and will need to choose a new dr.  Joined C4 but hasn''t received an official cancellation from Medicaid yet and needs the authorization # from the cancellation letter. They need to update their income on file to get the auth # first before we can continue with enrollment in this plan.  Tara''s portion of income is expected to be $25K in 2020 combined with Mark''s $75K.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-17 12:32:12', '2020-02-17 14:11:46'),
