  ('zcrm_1579374000046874003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002630141', 'Cameron Elmendorf', NULL, 'Referral check sent to Judson Rogers, husband of Lindsay Rogers.', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2020-02-12 08:56:16', '2020-02-12 08:56:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046863008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005173170', 'Melissa Smith', NULL, '***From the start of the welcome call Melissa was combative and confused.  She would stop  and ask me to elaborate on everything- meaning picking apart every work and asking for the definition behind it, because she told me that it sounded absolutely nothing like she thought she signed up for.  She had a huge problem with seeing the $3000 deductible associated with her RCI card- I explained it four times to her and she wouldn''t listen.  Without even getting off of page 1 of the script, and her not even able to confirm that she had chosen the member only $500 PSD.  So I let her know that I was as concerned as she was that we may have gotten what she chose wrong, that''s why we ask and verify at the beginning of the welcome call.  I asked her before continuing if she would like me to try and transfer her to Wendy- her response was " I never want to have to speak with that woman again."  And she asked me to continue, that maybe something would ring a bell.  So, I did.  She got very upset by the fact that I asked her if she had a HSA, she told me that, once again, she had never heard of that before, and asked me how it all worked- I once again, told her that it was concerting to me that she once again hadn''t heard of this- nor (was in her mind) explained and that it would be best if someone on our sales side go over this and everything else.  She said she wanted MY definition and that her sales person should''ve but didn''t go over it- all I could do was tell her my own experience with using many HSA''s in the past and that I loved it.  She said that it sounded like a stupid idea and that her accountant does all of that for her anyway- I told her that it would probably be beneficial if she reached out to her accountant about the idea to see what they would say.  
If I wanted to, which I don''t I could literally take Wendy''s welcome call script and mark the parts that set Melissa off the most.  If you have any questions about any of this please let me know- I will happily answer.
I think that the portion that goes over alternative care needing pre-approval first set her off for the grand finale.  Because she wanted me to spell it out for her over and over.  I heard that she was upset- and I would ask if she understood.  And she''d just say "continue"  after going over the HRA and then QR LIfe code, she expressed MORE doubts.  Saying- "this sounds nothing like what I thought I was getting" to which I reminded her that it might be- because sometimes things get lost in translation.  
She asked how could it be that she didn''t understand any of the names or phrases, and that''s when I asked her if she may have gone over the Redirect plan with her.  She said that it didn''t sound familiar and then asked what it was.  I went over it briefly, I told her that she may want to speak to Wendy concerning this- it may cut out some of the confusion for her.  
That''s when she told me that I shouldn''t judge her cognitive ability.  I told her that I wasn''t at all- that this plan can feel overwhelming to a lot of people and that is why the concierge service is there 9-9 est- to help walk members through something that is very new to them.  Then silence and faint crying- I asked her name and she told me that I triggered a combative nerve with her but to continue.  
I told her that I was sorry she crying, that I understood that it can be really overwhelming.  
I paused- because she''s crying!  and she just said "continue" 
"continue" 
at this point I felt like she had a gun to my head.  
there was silence for the rest of it until the end and she asked. "are we finished?" 
I said yes and she said "bye".
I felt completely beaten up by the end of the call.  
I have been up late typing all of this out- I am sorry if this is a bit choppy.  Please let me know if you have any questions. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-11 19:42:29', '2020-02-11 19:42:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046853053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047238273', 'Jennifer Bradfield', NULL, '2-11-20 Philip is 39 and wife Jennifer is 40. They are healthy and rarely go to Dr. Starting own biz and will no longer receive employer coverage. Full cost is $1800 a month with Anthem! Looked into Medishare also. Looking for March or April 1st start date. Will discuss with wife and get back to me. Very interested. PSDHC best since healthy family of 4. Kids are 9 and turning 7 next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-11 16:07:46', '2020-02-11 16:08:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046853038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047238442', 'Anne DeWaters', NULL, '2-11-20 Annie went to UVM! Looks like she''s friends with many of my friends as well. Perhaps know her through Meg McIntosh? Waiting for confirmed time to talk.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-11 15:22:21', '2020-02-11 15:22:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046853033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046972029', 'Erika Gutierrez', NULL, '2-11-20 Came through her boss  Catherine Brown. Catherine will pay up to $300 a month for Erika''s membership!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-11 15:14:00', '2020-02-11 15:14:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046853023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045539058', 'Allison Atkin', NULL, '2-11-20 Allison Atkin is Wendy Wassom''s 26 year old daughter, healthy, young, etc. Enrolled separately from Wendy.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-11 14:57:28', '2020-02-11 14:57:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046863003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001746009', 'Jill Bryant', NULL, 'Welcome call complete.  Address was her old address but she can still grab her welcome packet.  She is going to fill out a form.  Jill knows her stuff- she is still a little shell shocked due to her experiences with Liberty, but I assured her that she and Wendy made the best decision when it came to jumping onto Redirect. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-02-11 14:22:28', '2020-02-11 14:22:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046853013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000167696', 'Rachel Weitz', NULL, '2-11-20 Rachel was nervous bc Medicaid was never cancelled and they are showing she has double coverage with Medicaid and with C4 Kaiser. Told her to call Medicaid directly to update her records appropriately, show she''s married and doesn''t qualify for Medicaid. She''s getting APTC for Kaiser and is 37 weeks pregnant now. She''s afraid to mess anything up. I told her to make 100% certain her payments to Kaiser are up to date and ongoing and she said they are up to date. She will call Medicaid and sort it out. She''s doing her best to do it all correctly without any disruption in her coverage since due any day now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-11 13:51:35', '2020-02-11 13:51:35'),
