  ('zcrm_1579374000046238003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027361787', 'Cammy Dwyer-Abbey', NULL, 'Cammy has been communicating from the hospital in regards to the staff wanting her to take $7000 in medications- so she was wondering about the cost through Reid instead.  It was for an inhaler- I told her that he tends to get good prices on those and that we would just need the specifics.  I then reminded her of Reid''s contact info so that she could give him a call and kind of help her through with pricing out all of the medications.  She mentioned that staff have been pressuring her to get onto traditional insurance stat. - I sent Wendy the thread with that update, and told Cammy to reach out to us for any help. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-01-28 13:34:12', '2020-01-28 13:34:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046216069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046217362', 'Grace Lau', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $5000 IUA 50-59 DPC', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-28 13:03:04', '2020-01-28 13:03:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046223033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017830450', 'Debbie Eubanks', NULL, 'Debbie called in and had a few questions in regards to some bills for injury/illness and preventative. For the Injury/illness, she had some problems with her hip and needed to get a few different procedures done, with multiple appointments. She said she paid for everything out of pocket and did not know she wasn''t supposed to do that. She thought for a situation like that she pays for everything and then gets reimbursed. I told her no that is incorrect. She knew she has a $500 IUA but I guess she didn''t know to not pay more than that and to be billed the rest and submit to Sedera. I let her know of all of this and how it is supposed to work out. She understood after me telling her how it normally goes and posed the question of what to tell the providers when they tell her she HAS to pay upfront. I didn''t really know what else to tell her other than what the process is, that she tell them she has to be billed the rest and is not responsible for more than $500. She was a little put off about this so I went and asked Patti her opinion. She said the same thing and that this is something we should speak to Sedera about, I let Debbie know this and that I would get back to her after I hear back from Sedera about that. In the meantime I told her about submitting her bills to Sedera and all of her receipts as well. I sent her the email that explains how to do that and to call Sedera ASAP!! Their phone number is at the bottom of that email I sent. Secondly about her Preventative mammogram and bone density test she stated that this all happened back in June and she got both EOB''s from ASI stating her balance is $0 and she does now owe anything. The only issue is she said she is still getting bills from the provider and or facility for $306.22 which does not make any sense because ASI paid for all of it. I went over a couple things with her on what that could possibly be and we can''t seem to figure out what that is for and why they are still billing her. I asked if the bill she got has all the CPT codes and she said no it is just the statement saying what she owes. I told her to send that to me anyway and in the meantime get in contact with the provider and ask to send her the bill with the codes on them because that is what ASI is going to need to determine what is going on. She said she will do that and is going to call Sedera now about her reimbursement. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-01-28 12:56:26', '2020-01-28 12:56:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046216064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046217307', 'Heather Weidner', NULL, 'Member Only $500 IUA 30-39 PSD', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-28 12:53:48', '2020-01-28 12:53:48'),
