  ('zcrm_1579374000046220013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041823005', 'Angie Ward', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to reschedule the 30 minute welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-01-28 10:42:38', '2020-01-28 10:42:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046220008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042221122', 'Sarah Wright', NULL, 'Welcome call complete with Sarah and husband Bob. Member requested to be sent to her a Hippa complaint letter for husband to have access to her info. Sent it over to John to retrieve letter. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-01-28 10:36:29', '2020-01-31 08:02:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046216023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675095', 'Alvaro Hernandez', NULL, 'Belinda called in to Kelly and requested that this employee be cancelled she then submitted cancellation request.  I will cancel with ASi &amp; Sedera.  I cancelled billing.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-28 10:19:42', '2020-01-28 10:25:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046223023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447500', 'Clove Berger', NULL, 'Clove called in and said she had a few unresolved billing issues she wants to get resolved. The first 2 are from her husband getting kidney stones taken out, I stopped her and said that is injury/illness and anything with injury/illness is through Sedera and I can not see or have access to claims that are sent in with Sedera so she needs to get in contact with them and see where they are at with the process. She said she will give them a call. Last was billing from her mammogram. I explained to her the process of preventative and making sure the facility and provider are in the PHCS Network. She gave me the name of the facility and nothing was coming up so she said she will contact ASI and hung up. I was trying to let her know what type of bill she needs and was asking what she had already and she just hung up. I am assuming she is calling ASI. She did mention that she gave her ASI card and said that they sent it into the address on the back of her card. I am hoping it is the P.O. Box address for submitting claims. Again she hung up on me so that is all the help she is getting from me. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-01-28 10:15:42', '2020-01-28 10:15:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046216018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018451009', 'Kay Sasser', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation I will notify ASi &amp; Sedera Sunny cancelled billing.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-28 10:10:02', '2020-01-28 10:10:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046223018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675095', 'Alvaro Hernandez', NULL, 'I did not catch her name but a woman called in and said that one of her previous employees needs to be cancelled. Alvaro. She is the one that pays for everything and stated that Alvaro no longer works for them anymore so he needs to be cancelled. I told her I will send him and her the cancellation form via email. She said that is great and will get it back to us asap. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-01-28 09:44:55', '2020-01-28 09:44:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000046223013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740037', 'Lauren Wagner', NULL, 'Lauren called in and needed some assistance on how to use her plan. She said she has yet to utilize anything. She said that she needs to go see a cardiologist due to very high blood pressure and wanted to know the correct steps to take. I told her she called the correct place. I explained in full detail what she needs to do and that this is considered injury/illness, not preventative. With that being said she has no network and can go to any provider of her choosing. She will then present herself as a self pay patient up to her IUA of $500. I explained that her $500 is per Need. She will then ask to be billed the rest and to make sure she keeps every single receipt that is proof of payment to her IUA amount. She will get a cash discount by presenting herself this way. Once she has paid up to the $500 she will then ask to be billed the rest and will submit everything, including her receipts, to Sedera. Once Sedera has the proof of payment towards her IUA they will then contact the provider and negotiate the bill to a final cost. Once they have come to an agreement of cost Sedera will then send a check to her and Lauren will use that check to pay the provider. She fully understood everything I told her and was very very happy with my help. She asked on final question, say the cardiologist says they think she needs to go get an MRI or something along those line, send her somewhere else for other testing is it also going to be covered? I told her as long as this is for the same "Need" yes, she will not have to pay anything else or start over with her $500 because the further testing is for the same Need that she is dealing with. All she would have to do is get the bills and submit everything over to Sedera and they will help her with the rest of the process. Lauren was extremely grateful and happy with all the help and that I answered all her questions and more. Very happy with us and the customer service I always provide. We are all doing a GREAT job here at MPowering Benefits. She is used to getting the run around from tradition insurance and never can speak to a live person. She gets a live person every time she calls, even with our answering service if the lines are busy is a real person. She loves it and highly recommends us. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-01-28 09:41:24', '2020-01-28 09:41:24'),
