  ('zcrm_1579374000045760034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001881022', 'Carolyn Tabak', NULL, '1-14-20 Carolyn was complaining bc LHS is ruining her credit. But, she''d rather them ruin her credit and stick with them than pay $558-$610 a month for membership that still has pre-x. She''s dealing with mold toxicity called SIRS(?) otherwise known as chronic inflammation response syndrome. She sees a naturopath $275-$300 per hour. But, usually goes in for 30 min at around $150 which MIGHT be paid at least portion of that by Redirect. She''s willing to stick it out with LHS for now. We looked at C4HCO bc Financial Advisor is not supportive of health shares. Prices started $623 for worst Bright Health Bronze plan. She''s not interested in that and would rather die before she pays $8150 in medical expenses. So, C4 is not an option. She will feel things out with LHS for now. She asked about the Concierge to assist is managing bills but told her LHS doens''t allow others to speak on her behalf anymore, so not a good use of the Concierge. She also lives on $120K that she draws off her investments every year.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-01-14 11:43:19', '2020-01-14 11:45:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045747039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044406061', 'Mark Ovind', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Member needs to check if he received QR Life code card. Told him to call us if not received. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-01-14 11:28:52', '2020-01-14 11:28:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045758018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005956113', 'Desiree Brandt', NULL, 'Member called in bc of a Cancellation letter that Sunny sent her.  She told me that her wallet was stolen over the holidays.  She gave me a new card and I charged her so she is now up to date', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-14 11:21:01', '2020-01-14 11:21:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045760026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810797', 'Chris Massey', NULL, '1-14-20 Chris is thrilled to have his membership delayed until Feb. 1st and no further payment until Feb. 22nd for March membership. He knows he''s not protected for Jan. now. He said it will help a lot financially. Thanks Patti!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-01-14 11:06:10', '2020-01-14 11:07:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045760021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001165513', 'Christine Pietras', NULL, '1-14-20 Left vm for Christine letting her know Stmbt Rapid Care Clinic will qualify for the DPC discounted rate but will need to show proof of membership of course.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-01-14 11:00:17', '2020-01-14 11:00:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045761003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521236', 'Laura Chasko', NULL, 'Laura called in and she had a question on where she is supposed to submit a bill she got in the mail for her Annual Women''s Wellness Visit. I stopped her and asked the usual questions. Did she make sure the provider was in the PHCS Network? Yes. When I started to ask another question she stopped me and said she knows that the providers have to be in the PHCS Network but she did not want to get a new doctor and called ASI about this. She said she knows that they will only pay up to the 130% of medicare allowable. So her question was where does she send the bill. I told her 2 options. She can either do it herself and send it straight to ASI and the address is on the back of her ASI card, or she can send me the bill and I will email it to someone at ASI on her behalf. I made sure that she has the actual bill with the codes on them and she said yes and that she would rather me send the bill to someone. I told her that is no problem at all and gave her my email. I told her I will tag her in the thread as well. Next she said that she has to have a mammogram done and asked what the process is for that. I told her it is the same as what she would have done for the women''s visit. Find a provider in the PHCS Network and choose from the list I will send her. Told her to make sure when she is making the appt that she lets the people know it is strictly a Preventative Mammogram SCREENING. I made is clear that is can ONLY be the Screening. No 3D, Digital, or Tomography mammograms. Just the regular screening. Also the most important is making sure the providers code the billing as Preventative only for it to be covered at 100%. Lastly she is to bring her ASI card and present it to the front desk. I let her know there is a member support phone number for the receptionist to call and verify benefits with ASI. She 100% understood everything I told her, I could tell she got it. I let her know as well I will send a few other emails to her explaining everything I did so she doesn''t have to sit there and try and remember everything. Laura was very happy with my help and how easy everything is. She totally understands and acknowledges the fact that she is going to be paying out of pocket a certain percent for her women''s wellness visit cuz she did not stay in network. She is perfectly fine with that because she loves her Dr. and will not switch to anyone else unless she is forced to with her Dr. leaving or anything along those lines. But regardless very very happy member and is very smart and understanding of how everything goes. Willing to go through with all the steps needed for anything with the plan. I''d say a very MPowered Member hahaha :) ;) -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-01-14 10:55:30', '2020-01-14 10:55:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045747031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044904253', 'Marcella Friel', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-01-14 10:55:04', '2020-01-14 11:01:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045760008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045739067', 'Rachel Namordi', NULL, '1-14-20 Rachel is 43 and just divorced as of Jan. 7th. Self employed, contract worker making about $60-$70K in 2020. She''s healthy, no meds, no tobacco, no pre-x. Looked at Friday Health for $310, Anthem for $350. PSDHC is only $278 for $1500 IUA. Having her listen to the audio. Wants Dr. Melissa Coomes who is in network for PHCS. Kids will be on x''s plan.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-01-14 10:16:14', '2020-01-14 10:16:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045747026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810280', 'Alfred Shaw', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to book online the 30 minute welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-01-14 10:08:35', '2020-01-14 10:08:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045747021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810440', 'Erin Nissen', NULL, 'Spoke to member will book online the 30 minute welcome call. Sent email to do so. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2020-01-14 10:05:27', '2020-01-14 10:05:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045760003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003914005', 'Kevin West', NULL, '1-14-20 We have discussed switching away from LHS and we really need to stay on our budget right now (paying off our trip to Italy), so increasing our monthly premium by switching away from LHS is not very attractive right now. Since she has nothing urgent regarding her health she may elect to delay a few healthy visits and re-visit switching away from LHS later in 2020.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-01-14 09:52:29', '2020-01-14 09:52:29'),
