  ('zcrm_1579374000045363081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043354056', 'Richard Dalton', NULL, 'Per email below member is canceling because of the uncertainty involving a Pre-Ex condition.  Sounds like this was not explained clearly to the member at the time of sale because member is essentially saying the same thing about pre-ex.  I sent out link to cancellation form and will process when I receive.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-07 10:42:35', '2020-01-07 10:42:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000045363076', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043354056', 'Richard Dalton', NULL, 'Patti - Analisa Cleland suggested that I contact you.  I worked with Analisa to evaluate a number of health plan options.  I decide on the Sedera plan after asking a number of questions regarding the pre-existing conditions exclusions and getting feedback from Sedera (via Analisa) that my heart stent procedure would not be excluded after the third anniversary of the surgery.  After my first premium payment had processed I received an enrollment package (page 11 of Welcome to Sedera document) clearly stating that the pre-existing condition would be excluded 100% in the first year and pro-rate after that - based on the anniversary of our enrollment.  (Analisa further confirmed/clarified that withWendy Scipione of your office on January 3rd).  I can’t afford to take that potential risk/exposure financially and would like to cancel my policy/enrollment and request a refund of the premium I paid (I recognize the set up fee is non refundable). I would be happy to send the email chain of questions and responses that led to the confusion if you need further documentation to support my request.  Thank you for your help and consideration of this request.

Richard Dalton
rjladalton@gmail.com
303-903-0317', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-01-07 10:38:45', '2020-01-07 10:38:45'),
