  ('zcrm_1579374000044896020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026122744', 'Kimberly Payes', NULL, 'Kim called and she just needed a run down of how her plan works and what to do in certain situations. I pretty much broke down each portion of her plan and how it works. She is going to see a specialist for her knee right now because she had an accident while skiing over the weekend. I explained to her what is going to happen and what she does. I let her know that is considered Injury/Illness so it is not something that is covered. I told her she only pays up to $1000 out of pocket per her IUA. I told her there is no network and she can go to any provider of her choice. She will present herself as a cash pay patient and will most likely get a cash discount. I let her know that she will need to get in contact with Sedera and keep all her receipts and bills stating what she has paid. All those bills will be submitted to Sedera. I explained to her who they are and what Sedera does next after she has met her IUA. I sent her an email explaining how to submit her bills when the time comes. She spoke about possibly surgery. I told her that Sedera has a process that she will need to go through first before anything is done with a possible surgery. She fully understood all that. Then she said she has not used the plan at all yet for her yearly visits. So she asked me how it works with that and that she needs to have an OBGYN appointment and a Mammogram. I told her I will look up providers and facilities in her area and send her a list of in network providers via email attached as a PDF. I explained how she goes about making those appointments and was VERY VERY clear to her about HER making it clear that those appointments are Preventative ONLY and to make sure that everything is Coded as such as well. I also explained that she needs to bring her ASI card with her and there is a member support number for ASI on the back of the card that they front desk can call to verify benefits. She seemed to understand everything and was happy that I will be sending her emails with all this info and more included. Very happy member now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-23 12:21:31', '2019-12-23 12:21:31'),
