  ('zcrm_1579374000044844008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026209114', 'Kelly Shafer', NULL, 'Kelly has gotten an EOB from RCI stating that the charges for her annual mammogram that she made sure was preventative and went through all the correct steps in making sure of that, provider in the network, stating to the provider and front desk that it is strictly a preventative mammogram screening and to code everything as preventative and not have anything that would be considered diagnostic. I sent the EOB she attached for me over to Jennifer Chasteen at RCI. I got a response from a Lindsay Myers and this is the response that I got: Good afternoon,

 

After looking into this claim, we found that it hit our system incorrectly. This claim has been reprocessed, and the plan is paying the full allowed amount of $203.96. The member will be receiving an updated explanation of benefits once the payment is released to the provider.

 

Please let us know if you have any additional questions by calling the toll-free number provided below.

 

Thank you and have a wonderful day,

 

Lindsay Myers

Customer Service Rep. | 800.795.7772 - Toll Free

Lindsay.Myers@regionalcare.com

 SO at least half of her bill is getting paid for by RCI and she is at least happy with that and it is better than nothing. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-20 08:05:23', '2019-12-20 08:05:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044817083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810227', 'Rachel Thomas-Butts', NULL, 'Acct set up and January charged 12/20. Good to go for 1/1', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-12-20 08:03:44', '2019-12-20 08:03:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044844003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000039830081', 'Geraldine Gardner', NULL, 'Geraldine called in and asked if there was anyway for the charge that came out of her account this morning could be refunded because she put in a cancellation form this morning. She was deeply sorry to have to ask that and was going on about how amazing we have been and she really really does not want to cancel but financially she can not afford it right now. She spoke about how someone has financially ruiened her and there is just too much going on right now for her to be able to stay with us financially. She was very upset that she had to cancel and hopes that in the near future when things straighten out she will come back to us no question about it. She said we are the nicest people she has ever dealt with, especially when it comes to medical issues and "Insurance". She filled out the cancellation form and I spoke with Patti about getting the charge refunded and she said yes but it is going to take a little while longer than normal because of the holidays. But as soon as we physically get the money from her account we will refund it to her right away. She thanks us very much for all that we do and have done for her while she had the plan. Very grateful and she was so sweet about everything and thanked me a hundred times over and will be returning when she can! Very nice lady and everything is all set on our end for now until we return the charge. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-20 08:00:45', '2019-12-20 08:00:45'),
