  ('zcrm_1579374000044660023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044725004', 'Richard Zimmerman', NULL, '12-16-19 Ann and husband are choosing PSDHC with $1500/$655 IUA. Enrolling now. Referred by Dr. McClane Duncan Naturopathic Dr. from Siskiyou Vital Medicine in Bedford, OR. She thinks he''s a member of Sedera as well but he''s not with us. Ann also practices medicine herself so isn''t a member of Siskiyou. She is super sweet and super thankful. She recognizes this is the best option possible. Is cancelling her membership with LHS as soon as $125 is charged. She recognizes they have gone downhill fast.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-12-16 10:06:13', '2019-12-16 10:32:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044673008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000907023', 'Melinda Niemczyk', NULL, 'Melinda called in and had a bunch of questions on what is covered or not. First she wanted to know how the process is when needing to go have a colonoscopy because she just turned 60. I explained to her that yes that is something that is covered as long as it is strictly Preventative and coded as such. I then explained that the provider has to be in the PHCS network and I am the one that would do some research and send her a list of approved providers in her area via email. After that she would choose a provider from that list and make an appointment. I stressed to her to make sure she tells them that the appointment HAS to be Preventative only and billed and coded as such. Otherwise it will not be covered and can be a long process to get everything changed to Preventative and may not be able to change it if it indeed was Diagnostic. I explained to her what the differences are and how it can turn into that. She was very very sweet and patient with everything and fully understood what I was explaining to her and not getting frustrated or overwhelmed what so ever. I re assured her that I would be sending emails in relation to everything I was telling her so she did not have to sit there and try and remember every single thing I am telling her right now. That made her feel a lot better and happier :) She next had a question about whether or not for a woman that turned 60 like herself, if a Bone Density scan would be covered. She also said in relation to this, back in 2016 she had one and she was told she had Osteoporosis and if that would be considered pre-existing condition. I told her I would get back to her on those 2 questions because I was not 100% sure and would speak with one of my group admins and get her the correct answer. I got with John and he said that the only way the Bone Density would be covered 100% is if it was medically recommended by her provider and HAS to be coded as Preventative ONLY. Otherwise, no it would not be covered or considered preventative if her provider does not recommend it. Also for the 2016 diagnosis of Osteoporosis, no that is not considered pre-existing because of how long ago it was. I sent her the email explaining what to do and say on how to present herself at her preventative appointment for the colonoscopy, how to submit bills to Sedera with their phone number for her to call about opening a "Need" because she went in on Friday 12/13/19 to have a diagnostic mammogram and ultrasound and paid $450 our of her $500 IUA. I explained to her what she has to do next and call Sedera ASAP because she is very very close to her IUA and she knows she has to go back in and have an MRI done. I told her to keep all bills and receipts that show she paid the $450 so far and that she is going to have to submit those into Sedera and call them right away to start her first "Need". I will also be sending her the list of providers that I have found for a Gastroenterologist in her area for her Preventative Colonoscopy. She was very sweet and like I said extremely patient with me and was 100% understanding and said every little bit of information that I gave her today has been the biggest help and shows that I truly care about my members. She stated she loves the fact that I told her I would get back to her once I have talked with one of my group admins about the Bone Density test to get her the correct answer because with traditional insurance they just tell you what you want to hear and lie and said everything is covered. She said that one time she called in about some info if something was covered with her dental and they told her yes 100%. Come to find about 6 months later nothing was covered in reality and it was thousands and thousands of dollars that she didn''t have because she was made aware everything would have been covered. So she really appreciates that    I would go out of my way to make sure I get her the correct answer and not just wing it and make something up. I would never do that. Anyway, very sweet lady and she feels a LOT LOT more comfortable with all this info given and explained to her. Very happy Member!! -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-16 10:01:20', '2019-12-16 10:01:20'),
