  ('zcrm_1579374000044419023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003668018', 'Carol Ekeland', NULL, 'Member called in to cancel.  I will cancel her subscription as well - PB', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-10 11:56:19', '2019-12-10 11:56:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044419018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015086178', 'Kristine Smith', NULL, 'Member called in and asked if he needed to see someone in network to get a skin check.  I advised her that skin check were not part of the scope of preventative and that she could see anyone she wanted to for this and that it would be subject to her IUA.  Very manic lots of talking - PB', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-10 11:47:44', '2019-12-10 11:47:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044419013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610190', 'Andrea Lowery', NULL, 'Andrea called in and she needed help with a bill she got sent from her mammogram. I asked her a few questions. First off if she made sure the facility was in the PHCS Network. She did not know because she has always used this facility. When I looked up the name of the place she went to that was not coming up and I got 193 results. So I wrote down the name of the place and am going to call and see if they are in the PHCS network. I told her if she get me the EOB that has all the CPT codes on the bill to send over to ASI. All she has is statements that just say what she owes. John informed me that I can call ASI and give them some information and they can give me the EOB. I will stay in contact with Andrea once I have gotten more info for her and she will let me know when she gets the, what I told her we call it is the "Super Bill". she will let me know and I will keep her and notes updated on to what is going on.   -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-10 11:12:35', '2019-12-10 11:12:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044419008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027786019', 'Amber Senator', NULL, 'Amber called and wanted to know what the process is and if it is something that is covered to make and appointment for getting prescribed an epi pen. I let her know that no that is not preventative and she will be paying out of pocket up to her IUA of $500, nothing more than that. I explained what she needs to do if her bill exceeds that IUA and how Sedera comes into play at that point. I told her to keep all statements and receipts that prove she paid and met her IUA. I sent her an email that explains how to submit her bills and that Sedera''s phone number is in there if she has any other questions on what to do. She also asked how she goes about looking up a provider for when the time comes for Preventative appointments. I explained that she calls into me here and tells me what type of provider she is looking for and I will do some research and pull up a list of providers that are in the PHCS Network and send her the list via email as a PDF. I sent her an email as well that explains how she will present herself for those preventative appointments. She seemed to understand what I have told her and thanked me very much for the information and will be looking for those emails. She will give me a call in the near future to look up some providers for her.  -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-10 11:09:11', '2019-12-10 11:09:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000044419003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011508059', 'Marla Ratcliff', NULL, 'Marla called in to just make sure she was doing the correct thing with making her appointment for her annual preventative women''s wellness visit. I looked up her provider and she is good to go on that end, they ARE in the PHCS network. She said to me that she tells them to make sure that it is strictly Preventative and the billing is also coded as such, NOT Diagnostic. She fully understands what she needs to do. Just be super safe I told her I will be sending her an email that explains how she is going to present herself upon arrival at her appointment. I also sent her the 64+ Preventative services that are mandated by the ACA and what she is able to do with her plan. Her last question was about a need that she opened up Jan 2019 and wanted to know is come the date of her first opening is a year later if it is going to close and she needs to start over again. To be sure John looked at her Sedera Needs profile and checked what was going on with that, and John let me know that no it will not close and re open. I called Marla back to let her know and left a voicemail that she is all set and does not need to worry about re opening the need. It will close once everything has be completed and processed. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-12-10 10:45:23', '2019-12-10 10:45:23'),
